---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
---

<Layout title="About | Prima Veritas">

<main class="flex-1">

  <PageHero
    title="About"
    subtitle="Operational experience informing deterministic infrastructure design."
  />

  <Section title="What Prima Veritas Is">
    <p>
      Prima Veritas reconstructs operational history from fragmented system data and produces
      a hash-chained record that can be rechecked without the original systems.
    </p>
    <p>
      It does not replace existing systems, analyze performance, or interpret outcomes.
      It establishes a single, consistent account of what actually happened.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Why It Exists">
    <p>
      Operational systems rarely produce a complete or consistent history on their own.
    </p>
    <p>
      Data is split across tools, transformed over time, and often contains gaps or
      inconsistencies. Reconstructing events requires manual effort, assumptions, and
      cross-team coordination.
    </p>
    <p>
      This creates friction in audits, investigations, and day-to-day operations where
      accuracy matters.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prima Veritas is designed to reduce that ambiguity by producing a record that is
      consistent and reproducible.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="How It Approaches the Problem">
    <p>
      Prima Veritas converts raw system data into a structured sequence of events and
      preserves that sequence exactly as it occurred.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each event is linked to the next, forming a continuous chain. If events inside a sealed
      record are changed or reordered, the structure no longer aligns.
    </p>
    <p>
      Removing events from the end, or replacing the whole record, is detectable only against
      a receipt kept separately.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Verification Model">
    <p>
      Every reconstruction produces a portable, sealed bundle identified by its SHA-256 hash.
    </p>
    <p>
      The bundle can be rechecked without access to the original systems that produced the
      data. Checking it against a hash kept separately shows whether it has changed since it
      was sealed.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Roadmap (in development, not yet available)">
    <p>
      Planned capabilities built on the same underlying record: replaying events, generating
      structured reports, and tracing relationships across systems.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Philosophy">
    <p>
      Prima Veritas is built on a simple principle:
    </p>
    <p class="text-off-white">
      Accurate decisions require an accurate understanding of what already happened.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most systems focus on collecting data or producing outputs. Few ensure that the
      historical record itself is consistent.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prima Veritas treats operational history as a first-class problem.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <!-- FOUNDERS — bare for custom layout -->
  <Section title="Founders" bare last={true}>
    <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl space-y-10">

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-sans tracking-tight text-off-white">Bryan Ziehl</h3>
        <div class="mt-4 text-sm text-off-white/80 space-y-4">
          <p>
            Independent systems builder focused on reconstructing and verifying operational
            history across fragmented data sources.
          </p>
          <p>
            Background includes maritime operations and real-world systems where incomplete
            or conflicting records create risk, ambiguity, and operational friction.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-sans tracking-tight text-off-white">Brookes Drew</h3>
        <div class="mt-4 text-sm text-off-white/80 space-y-4">
          <p>
            Operator with experience in maritime and logistics environments where accurate
            historical records are critical for coordination, compliance, and accountability.
          </p>
          <p>
            Focuses on applying structured data reconstruction to real-world operational systems.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </Section>

</main>

</Layout>